_[#057da]"],"description":"The magic happens with this single neuron, activated when something is detected by the distance sensor in front of SpikerBot.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775498551724","neuronKeys":["[#d213d]"],"edgeStrings":["[#d213d]_#_[#057da]","[#d213d]_#_[#bc0f2]"],"description":"When the bottom neuron is excitatory, it sends spikes to the forward motion of both motors. This adds to the rotation, and causes SpikerBot to drive towards its target.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775498596507","neuronKeys":["[#293b9]","[#d213d]"],"edgeStrings":["[#d213d]_#_[#293b9]","[#293b9]_#_[#de24f]","[#293b9]_#_[#07e41]"],"description":"When the excitatory neuron is active, it will also supress the neurons from driving the motors in reverse by using the inhibitory neuron downstream. This ensures it is always on the hunt.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775498658246","neuronKeys":["[#d213d]"],"edgeStrings":[],"description":"Try changing this neuron from Excitatory to Inhibitory! You will see its color change from mostly black to mostly white.","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775498760612","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#d213d]_#_[#293b9]","[#d213d]_#_[#bc0f2]","[#d213d]_#_[#057da]"],"description":"If the bottom neuron has been changed to Inhibitory, we will supress forward motion on the turning signals, and it will not trigger the neuron that stops reverse motion. SpikerBot will face the target, but will back up with fear if it gets too close!","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Predator or Prey","description":"Change the bottom neuron from excitatory to inhibitory to change personalities!","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:33:08.216174"}}